.TH elf_section_size 3 "ELF Library Functions" "QuickJS" "ELF Library Functions"

.SH NAME
elf_section_size \- Retrieve the size of a section by its index

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/elf.h>
.B size_t elf_section_size(void* elf, int sn);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B elf_section_size function retrieves the size of a section by its index.

The function takes two parameters:
.I elf
A pointer to the ELF file structure.
.I sn
The index of the section to find.

The function returns the size of the section if it is found. If the section is not found, the function returns 0.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B elf_section_size function:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/elf.h>

int main() {
  // Assume elf is a valid pointer to an ELF file structure
  int sn = 1; // Example section index
  size_t size = elf_section_size(elf, sn);

  if (size != 0) {
    printf("Section size: %zu\n", size);
  } else {
    printf("Section not found.\n");
  }

  return 0;
}
.!
